# Canonical line ending for this repository: LF in the index and in the working tree.
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise rewrite the
# working tree to CRLF on the next checkout and leave it inconsistent with the LF
# index: diffs become platform-dependent and byte-level comparisons break.
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect and skip binary files.
* text=auto eol=lf
